<title>UK: Sema says BAeSema not in BAe/Lagardere bid.</title>
<headline>Sema says BAeSema not in BAe/Lagardere bid.</headline>
<dateline>LONDON 1997-05-07</dateline>
<text>
<p>Anglo-French electronics and computer services company Sema Group Plc said on Wednesday that its BAeSema joint venture with British Aerospace Plc was not included in a proposed joint venture between BAe and France's Lagardere.  </p>
<p>Lagardere and rival Alcatel Alsthom Cie Generale earlier submitted their final bids for Thomson-CSF, which is being sold off by the French government.</p>
<p>BAe has said it agreed with Lagardere that their missile joint venture Matra BAE Dynamics would take over Bae and Thomson naval businesses if Lagardere's bid for Thomson-CSF was successful.</p>
<p>-- London newsroom +44 171 542 7717</p>
</text>
